%N A400975 Start with a set of four adjacent collinear points in a hexagonal lattice. Every iteration, add to the set the lattice points which are adjacent to exactly two points already in the set. This sequence gives the number of points in the set after n iterations.
%C A400975 Starting with two points yields A338097, and starting with an odd number k of adjacent collinear points produces a sequence that terminates after k-1 iterations. For example, starting with five such points yields 5,13,23,27,33,33,33,... . If we start with any number k of adjacent collinear points, then for n = 0,1,...,k-1, the number of points after n iterations is k + n*(2*k-n+1) - 2*(n mod 2).
